## [17_ids_and_transaction_matching — IDs and Transaction Matching]

Status: Major Revisions

### Accuracy Audit

* AWID/BID and ARID/RID correlation is directionally correct.
* “The slave mirrors the exact ID” applies to the ID accepted at that local subordinate interface. An interconnect can widen, remap, or privately retain source identity and must restore the originating interface’s ID on the response path.
* RID does not by itself “close out” a read transaction. A read retires only when the accepted R beat also has RLAST asserted.
* BID retires one write only when `BVALID && BREADY` occurs.
* IDs are not required to be unique across all outstanding transactions. The same ID can be reused and creates a per-ID issue-order queue.
* The lesson omits WID completely:

  * AXI3 includes WID and can support write-data interleaving.
  * AXI4 removes WID.
  * AXI4 write-data bursts follow write-address transaction order.
