* Same-ID read responses and same-ID write responses must preserve their applicable issue order.
* Different IDs have no relative response-order guarantee.
* Different-ID read beats can be interleaved where the connected components support interleaving.
* The lesson must distinguish:

  * Response order at an interface.
  * Internal target execution order.
  * Memory visibility and side-effect order.
* Same numeric IDs on the read and write channels do not create read/write ordering.
* The explanation that the master would misattribute reversed same-ID responses is useful, but same-ID ordering is a protocol obligation, not merely an implementation convenience.
